WEBVTT

00:00.264 --> 00:03.588
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:03.688 --> 00:06.990
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.025 --> 00:10.693
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.729 --> 00:13.930
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.965 --> 00:16.766
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:16.802 --> 00:20.403
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.439 --> 00:21.971
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.007 --> 00:23.807
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.842 --> 00:24.297
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.824 --> 00:36.038
Peter, we got to talk.

00:36.039 --> 00:36.634
Ugh.

00:36.635 --> 00:39.260
I'm concerned about
Stewie's preschool.

00:39.261 --> 00:41.395
Look what they're serving
at snack time.

00:41.429 --> 00:42.895
Is-is that...?

00:42.931 --> 00:44.130
It's dog milk.

00:44.165 --> 00:46.132
They're serving dog
milk to our children.

00:46.167 --> 00:48.067
Aw, sweet, dilk.

00:48.102 --> 00:50.169
I don't want Stewie
in that school anymore.

00:50.205 --> 00:52.205
It seems like it's
really gone downhill.

00:52.240 --> 00:53.773
She's not wrong to worry.

00:53.808 --> 00:55.308
There's a sign
in the bathroom that says,

00:55.343 --> 00:57.343
"If it's brown, let it mellow."

00:57.378 --> 00:59.312
Sometimes it crests
the toilet lid.

00:59.347 --> 01:01.781
Peter, I think we should
send Stewie to Corridors.

01:01.816 --> 01:03.015
I know it's
a little pricey,

01:03.051 --> 01:04.650
but it's the best
preschool in the area.

01:04.686 --> 01:06.819
Really? Is that the one
where they make 'em dress

01:06.855 --> 01:09.388
in the little shorts and hats
like the guy in AC/DC?

01:09.424 --> 01:10.890
Yeah, why does he
wear that outfit?

01:10.925 --> 01:12.391
'Cause he rocks.

01:14.596 --> 01:15.962
When I picked this,

01:15.997 --> 01:19.532
I didn't know I'd have
to wear it when I'm 60!

01:19.567 --> 01:21.734
I'm very cold!

01:26.474 --> 01:28.641
You know what seems
like a lie to me?

01:28.676 --> 01:31.210
A Forever stamp that says
"Love" on it.

01:31.246 --> 01:33.312
Oh, you want to
go ahead of me?

01:33.348 --> 01:34.413
Hey, how are you?

01:34.449 --> 01:36.949
You know what seems
like a lie to me?

01:36.985 --> 01:39.352
I can help the fourth
person in line.

01:39.387 --> 01:41.721
One, two, three... yes!

01:41.756 --> 01:44.056
Cleveland,
you work here?

01:44.092 --> 01:46.359
Yup, finally landed
myself a job.

01:46.394 --> 01:48.995
Hey, what can
Brown do for you?

01:50.098 --> 01:51.397
That's our
competitor, though.

01:51.432 --> 01:52.899
I'm not supposed
to say that.

01:52.934 --> 01:55.735
It's grounds for dismissal
if anyone ever got fired here,

01:55.770 --> 01:56.736
but they don't.

01:56.771 --> 01:58.204
Well, good for you.

01:58.239 --> 01:59.972
Oh, could I get a
return receipt for this?

02:00.008 --> 02:02.808
It's Stewie's registration
form for his new school.

02:02.844 --> 02:04.610
Lil' Papa Stew-Stew's
off to college?

02:04.646 --> 02:05.878
No, just preschool.

02:05.914 --> 02:07.013
He's very young.

02:07.048 --> 02:09.448
Can you just charge me
my weirdly uneven price

02:09.484 --> 02:10.650
so I can be done?

02:10.685 --> 02:13.185
All right, that's $2.16.

02:13.221 --> 02:16.923
$4.37 if you want to
send it the priority.

02:16.958 --> 02:19.058
Oh, no, we got to start
saving our pennies

02:19.093 --> 02:21.193
now that we're sending
Stewie to a new school.

02:21.229 --> 02:23.396
I'm actually doing some
job hunting after this.

02:23.431 --> 02:24.564
Let's go up there!

02:24.599 --> 02:26.699
You know, Lois,
the post office is hiring.

02:26.734 --> 02:27.700
Really?

02:27.735 --> 02:29.435
Oh, wow, that'd be great.

02:29.470 --> 02:31.671
Yeah, I'd be happy to
get you an interview,

02:31.706 --> 02:34.173
and as a white woman,
you'd be a minority here,

02:34.208 --> 02:36.409
unless you're an alcoholic.

02:47.021 --> 02:49.522
Wow, this place
is really fancy.

02:49.557 --> 02:52.191
Their Flat Stanley is
actually award-winning actor

02:52.226 --> 02:53.426
Stanley Tucci.

02:53.461 --> 02:57.263
Sometimes I wear glasses
and sometimes I don't.

02:57.298 --> 02:58.864
Hi, I'm Chadley.

02:58.900 --> 03:00.199
I've been kidnapped
three times

03:00.234 --> 03:01.467
because I come
from money.

03:01.502 --> 03:03.269
Oh, yes, I've heard
about your family.

03:03.304 --> 03:05.404
You've had two older
brothers die of drugs?

03:05.440 --> 03:06.405
That's right.

03:06.441 --> 03:07.607
Stewie, what would you say

03:07.642 --> 03:09.308
to a playdate at
my house tomorrow?

03:09.344 --> 03:11.444
That sounds delightful.

03:11.479 --> 03:14.647
My word, it feels so good
to finally be where I belong.

03:14.682 --> 03:17.783
Like Judd Hirsch at
the gigantic sweater store.

03:17.819 --> 03:20.620
Hi, uh, all five of us
are Judd Hirsch.

03:20.655 --> 03:22.989
Do you have a sweater big
enough to fit all of us?

03:24.459 --> 03:26.325
Okay, everybody climb in.

03:27.495 --> 03:30.596
Ah, I can't wait
to spill soup on this.

03:30.632 --> 03:33.466
Okay, Judds, shamble away.

03:38.373 --> 03:39.939
Good having
you aboard, Lois.

03:39.974 --> 03:41.707
Let me show you around.

03:41.743 --> 03:42.875
That guy right there?

03:42.910 --> 03:43.876
Larry.

03:43.911 --> 03:45.011
Okay, got it.

03:45.046 --> 03:46.012
A-And what's this giant,

03:46.047 --> 03:47.013
empty,

03:47.048 --> 03:48.914
football-stadium-sized room?

03:48.950 --> 03:50.883
Oh, the post office
anticipates

03:50.918 --> 03:52.551
that within the
next five years

03:52.587 --> 03:55.354
at least 200 million men
in this country will be

03:55.390 --> 03:57.723
ordering and
receiving RealDolls.

03:57.759 --> 04:00.559
Every man will have seven
to nine RealDolls.

04:00.595 --> 04:02.662
Asians, blonde
Southern girls,

04:02.697 --> 04:04.830
blonde Asians
capable of performing

04:04.866 --> 04:06.799
every possible sexual act,

04:06.834 --> 04:08.868
or at least
incapable of refusing.

04:08.903 --> 04:10.302
You can put one
in your car

04:10.338 --> 04:12.805
and drive in the car pool
lane with it and then

04:12.840 --> 04:15.508
maybe you push her head down,
thus defeating the purpose

04:15.543 --> 04:17.877
of the car pool lane while
fulfilling the purpose

04:17.912 --> 04:19.145
of the RealDoll.

04:19.180 --> 04:20.546
Maybe a trucker goes by.

04:20.581 --> 04:23.215
You say, "Hey, Janine,
give him a show."

04:23.251 --> 04:25.985
Maybe later you ask yourself
some tough questions, like,

04:26.020 --> 04:27.687
"Why is it so
important to you

04:27.722 --> 04:29.455
to impress and
excite truckers?"

04:29.490 --> 04:31.257
Anyhoo, grab that
letter opener.

04:31.292 --> 04:34.160
I'm gonna show you why you
should never mail cash.

04:37.699 --> 04:39.565
Another good postal tip is,

04:39.600 --> 04:41.500
if you wait to deliver
your mail at night,

04:41.536 --> 04:44.203
you can smell a lot
of really nice dinners.

04:44.238 --> 04:46.972
Oh, no, it's that
Amazon drone.

04:47.008 --> 04:48.240
Try to ignore it.

04:48.276 --> 04:49.842
Hey, Cleveland,
what are you doing?

04:49.877 --> 04:50.910
Taking a walk?

04:50.945 --> 04:52.545
No, I'm delivering mail.

04:52.580 --> 04:53.546
By foot?

04:53.581 --> 04:55.214
Yeah, that won't take too long.

04:55.249 --> 04:56.382
Well, got to go.

04:56.417 --> 05:00.219
Got to deliver these fat pants
to your fat son.

05:00.254 --> 05:02.488
He was harsh but
not untruthful.

05:02.523 --> 05:04.590
We got to special-order
Cleveland Jr.'s pants

05:04.625 --> 05:07.893
from a company that
manufactures grill covers.

05:13.000 --> 05:14.366
Thanks for coming
over, Stewie.

05:14.402 --> 05:15.534
Oh, thanks
for having me.

05:15.570 --> 05:16.969
Quite a place
you've got here.

05:17.004 --> 05:18.304
Your mother seemed nice.

05:18.339 --> 05:21.107
Yeah, I've only met her
a couple of times, but yeah.

05:21.142 --> 05:22.341
This is my bedroom.

05:26.647 --> 05:29.215
Is that car bed
a Bentley?

05:29.250 --> 05:30.649
And is that guy
the driver?

05:30.685 --> 05:33.452
Ready for this evening's
trip to Snoozetown, sir?

05:33.488 --> 05:34.453
Not yet.

05:34.489 --> 05:35.489
Sad story.

05:35.523 --> 05:36.889
He used to drive the bed

05:36.924 --> 05:38.224
for Michael
Jackson's monkey.

05:38.259 --> 05:40.326
I've seen some
terrible things.

05:40.361 --> 05:41.794
This is extraordinary.

05:41.829 --> 05:43.195
Oh, it's fine,
I suppose,

05:43.231 --> 05:44.463
but you probably have

05:44.499 --> 05:46.232
even nicer things
at your mansion.

05:46.267 --> 05:47.900
I'd love to come
see it sometime.

05:47.935 --> 05:50.136
Oh, um, y-yes,
yes, my mansion.

05:50.171 --> 05:52.338
Y-Yes, you-you should
come see my mansion,

05:52.373 --> 05:53.472
b-by all means.

05:53.508 --> 05:54.740
I mean, not-not
right this minute.

05:54.776 --> 05:57.076
I-I have the U.S.
men's wrestling team there--

05:57.111 --> 05:58.210
I'm gonna kill a wrestler--

05:58.246 --> 05:59.445
but then after that,
you should.

05:59.480 --> 06:00.780
I can't wait.

06:00.815 --> 06:02.848
Come on, let's go see if
the maid brought her son,

06:02.884 --> 06:05.484
so we can push him and
he can't do anything.

06:05.520 --> 06:08.020
God, I like it here,
but what am I doing?

06:08.055 --> 06:09.522
I don't have a fancy house.

06:09.557 --> 06:12.258
I'm living a lie, like FDR.

06:12.293 --> 06:17.062
And so I say to you, America,
we are going to win this war,

06:17.098 --> 06:19.098
we're going to end
this depression,

06:19.133 --> 06:22.535
and there's no reason
to suspect that I cannot walk.

06:22.570 --> 06:24.537
God bless America!

06:28.543 --> 06:29.575
And cut.

06:29.610 --> 06:30.610
The newsreel's over.

06:30.645 --> 06:32.411
Thank you, Mr. President.

06:32.446 --> 06:33.913
You're welcome, gentlemen.

06:33.948 --> 06:37.449
Now, if you'd kindly kick me
into the closet with the mops.

06:40.922 --> 06:43.422
Ah, must be a Yale man.

06:43.457 --> 06:44.723
Shut up.

06:48.429 --> 06:50.429
Hello, loyal mailwoman.

06:50.464 --> 06:52.164
This is a letter
to Hollywood,

06:52.200 --> 06:55.000
saying, "Keep it up!
Movies are great!"

06:56.037 --> 06:58.003
Cleveland, what should
I do with this?

06:58.039 --> 06:59.972
I-It just says
"Hollywood, U.S.A.,"

07:00.007 --> 07:01.340
and this isn't a stamp,

07:01.375 --> 07:03.008
it's the little
sticker from an apple.

07:03.044 --> 07:04.677
Oh, I can't never
get those off.

07:04.712 --> 07:05.712
I just eat them.

07:05.746 --> 07:07.346
Anyway, just put
it in here.

07:07.381 --> 07:08.414
But what's that?

07:08.449 --> 07:09.748
It's the dead letter bin.

07:09.784 --> 07:12.518
It's all the stale mail
what never got delivered

07:12.553 --> 07:15.754
for one reason or the other:
incomplete addresses,

07:15.790 --> 07:18.858
house at the top of a hill,
anyone who uses one of those

07:18.893 --> 07:21.093
French sevens with
a slash in it.

07:21.128 --> 07:22.428
Well, this is horrible.

07:22.463 --> 07:23.729
I'm going to organize these.

07:23.764 --> 07:25.264
There might be some
we could resend.

07:25.299 --> 07:26.999
That's above
and beyond, Lois.

07:27.034 --> 07:29.201
You know, you do
the uniform proud,

07:29.237 --> 07:30.636
like I like to think I--

07:30.671 --> 07:32.938
oh, chili dog got me.

07:32.974 --> 07:33.939
Look at all these.

07:33.975 --> 07:35.007
This is a mess.

07:35.042 --> 07:37.610
Here's two that
are stuck together.

07:37.645 --> 07:39.011
What the hell?

07:39.046 --> 07:40.179
This is from Peter.

07:43.484 --> 07:45.818
Who the hell is Gretchen Mercer?

07:45.853 --> 07:49.255
And this is postmarked
a week before our wedding!

07:54.328 --> 07:56.962
Aw, there was a time
when the president

07:56.998 --> 08:00.266
of the Jonathan Taylor Thomas
Fan Club got a lot of mail.

08:06.187 --> 08:08.081
I don't know
what to do, Bonnie.

08:08.082 --> 08:09.548
Why would Peter
write a letter

08:09.583 --> 08:12.151
to another woman
just before our wedding?

08:12.186 --> 08:14.019
Why don't you just
open it and read it?

08:14.055 --> 08:15.055
What?!

08:15.089 --> 08:16.422
Th-That's a
federal offense.

08:16.457 --> 08:17.756
I can't do that.

08:17.792 --> 08:19.491
Don't you realize,
as a postal employee,

08:19.527 --> 08:22.294
I'm 6,004th in line
for the presidency?

08:22.329 --> 08:24.129
Well, then why don't you
just deliver the letter

08:24.165 --> 08:27.066
and see for yourself
who this Gretchen Mercer is?

08:27.101 --> 08:29.001
Bonnie,
that's a great idea.

08:29.036 --> 08:31.036
Although it could be
a little awkward.

08:31.072 --> 08:33.338
You could always just
ask Peter about it.

08:33.374 --> 08:35.507
No, he won't talk
about anything serious

08:35.543 --> 08:37.042
unless there's
a crackling fire

08:37.078 --> 08:40.012
to punctuate uncomfortable
family revelations.

08:42.516 --> 08:44.116
I didn't fall
off the roof.

08:44.151 --> 08:45.651
I jumped.

08:47.154 --> 08:48.887
I never found
you attractive,

08:48.923 --> 08:51.190
and what's more,
I never respected you.

08:52.760 --> 08:54.726
I know about Maurice.

08:57.231 --> 08:59.598
Which Maurice?

09:03.471 --> 09:05.437
Oh, Brian,
I need your help!

09:05.473 --> 09:07.272
Chadley wants to
have a playdate,

09:07.308 --> 09:08.373
here at my house!

09:08.409 --> 09:10.142
Well, that's great.
No, it's not!

09:10.177 --> 09:11.543
I can't let him
see this dump.

09:11.579 --> 09:14.480
Come on, Stewie, Chadley should
like you for who are.

09:14.515 --> 09:16.081
Besides, this place
isn't so bad.

09:16.117 --> 09:19.284
Brian, Chadley's parents
each have their own bathroom.

09:19.320 --> 09:21.854
I've seen the fat man
pee through Lois' legs

09:21.889 --> 09:23.388
while she's sitting
on the toilet.

09:23.424 --> 09:25.524
What I've got to do
is find a spectacular house

09:25.559 --> 09:28.026
that I can pretend is mine
to impress Chadley.

09:28.062 --> 09:29.828
Oh, why don't you just
use Babs and Carter's?

09:29.864 --> 09:30.996
I can't, they're having

09:31.031 --> 09:33.098
<i>an Eyes Wide Shut
party all weekend.</i>

09:33.134 --> 09:35.567
I can't find my wiener
with this mask.

09:35.603 --> 09:36.568
All right, time-out.

09:36.604 --> 09:38.036
Let's-let's all just find

09:38.072 --> 09:40.439
our wieners and then
put the masks back on.

09:45.779 --> 09:48.881
Okay, 940,
this is the house.

09:51.051 --> 09:53.152
Hi, are you
Gretchen Mercer?

09:53.187 --> 09:54.553
Yes, may I help you?

09:54.588 --> 09:59.224
Oh, yeah, we found an old
letter addressed to you.

09:59.260 --> 10:00.792
Peter Griffin?

10:00.828 --> 10:02.961
Wow, this is from
an old boyfriend.

10:02.997 --> 10:04.029
What?

10:05.366 --> 10:07.366
Wow, well, um,
here-here's the nutty thing:

10:07.401 --> 10:08.567
believe it or not,

10:08.602 --> 10:11.470
I'm actually married
to Peter Griffin right now.

10:11.505 --> 10:14.006
Huh, that is quite
a coincidence.

10:14.041 --> 10:16.108
I wonder why he
was writing me.

10:18.145 --> 10:19.444
I see you move
your finger along

10:19.480 --> 10:20.445
as you read.

10:20.481 --> 10:22.114
That's what
little kids do.

10:22.149 --> 10:23.348
Oh, it was nothing.

10:23.384 --> 10:25.517
He was just writing
to say that he was excited

10:25.553 --> 10:27.753
about getting married
and that he finally had enough

10:27.788 --> 10:30.789
Camel Cash to get a leather
jacket and a pool floatie.

10:30.824 --> 10:32.591
Huh, well,
thank you, Gretchen.

10:32.626 --> 10:34.059
I am very relieved.

10:34.094 --> 10:35.360
I was thinking the worst.

10:35.396 --> 10:36.662
Oh, I understand,

10:36.697 --> 10:38.830
but you have nothing
to worry about.

10:38.866 --> 10:39.831
You're right.

10:39.867 --> 10:41.934
I guess jealousy's
my weak spot.

10:41.969 --> 10:43.435
Everyone has one.

10:43.470 --> 10:44.870
Even Achilles.

10:44.905 --> 10:47.439
So, you can only be injured
on your Achilles' tendon?

10:47.474 --> 10:48.474
That's right.

10:48.509 --> 10:50.075
My mother dipped me
into the River Styx

10:50.110 --> 10:51.577
and she held me by my heels,

10:51.612 --> 10:53.612
so that's the only part
that can be injured.

10:53.647 --> 10:55.047
How about you, Testiclies?

10:55.082 --> 10:57.849
It's the same--
it's-it's-it's similar.

11:05.726 --> 11:07.659
So, what do you think
of the house, Brian?

11:07.695 --> 11:09.861
As far as Chadley knows,
this is where I live.

11:09.897 --> 11:11.230
Stewie, who owns
this place?

11:11.265 --> 11:13.198
Oh, just some rich
idiot I saw bragging

11:13.234 --> 11:15.067
about his vacation
on Instagram.

11:15.102 --> 11:17.469
He posted a picture
of his feet in sand.

11:17.504 --> 11:19.104
You're a guy,
don't do that.

11:19.139 --> 11:20.239
What a dick.

11:20.274 --> 11:21.974
Hey, I'll swallow
his dental floss.

11:22.009 --> 11:22.975
You pull it out of me

11:23.010 --> 11:23.976
and put it back
on the roll.

11:24.011 --> 11:24.977
Good call.

11:26.013 --> 11:27.246
Ah, that must be Chadley.

11:28.616 --> 11:29.581
Hi, Stewie.

11:29.617 --> 11:30.749
I love your house.

11:30.784 --> 11:31.850
Where are your servants?

11:31.885 --> 11:33.418
Oh, probably
cooking bananas

11:33.454 --> 11:34.820
and doing the
cha-cha-cha.

11:34.855 --> 11:37.189
You know, this is a
great house for a party.

11:37.224 --> 11:38.890
You could invite
the whole class.

11:38.926 --> 11:40.892
I-I say,
that's a brilliant idea!

11:40.928 --> 11:42.127
What the hell
are you doing?

11:42.162 --> 11:44.263
Relax, these people
are gone for a few more days.

11:44.298 --> 11:45.330
I'll invite everyone over

11:45.366 --> 11:47.599
and impress the whole
class in one shot.

11:47.635 --> 11:49.735
That'll cover my
playdates for a year.

11:49.770 --> 11:50.902
You really think
that'll work?

11:50.938 --> 11:52.004
Absolutely.

11:52.039 --> 11:54.072
And when it does,
I'll be as popular

11:54.108 --> 11:55.240
as the first kid in school

11:55.276 --> 11:56.742
to get his driver's license.

11:56.777 --> 11:59.311
Hey, heard you
got your license.

11:59.346 --> 12:00.445
Maybe after school,

12:00.481 --> 12:02.547
you could take me
to get some groceries?

12:02.583 --> 12:05.284
Yeah, or maybe you and me
hop in that car of yours

12:05.319 --> 12:07.252
and do some
grocery shopping?

12:07.288 --> 12:09.788
Looks like you have
a roomy backseat.

12:09.823 --> 12:13.091
I'd love to fill that
with groceries after school.

12:13.127 --> 12:14.593
Hey, it's Stewie.

12:14.628 --> 12:17.729
All I know about cars
is what my mom does.

12:24.371 --> 12:25.771
Gretchen?!

12:25.806 --> 12:27.105
Wow, you look great!

12:27.141 --> 12:28.640
Yeah, I didn't have kids.

12:28.676 --> 12:30.008
Oh, yeah, of course,

12:30.044 --> 12:31.443
but what the hell
are you doing here?!

12:31.478 --> 12:33.145
I haven't seen
you in 20 years!

12:33.180 --> 12:35.314
Peter, I finally got
your letter.

12:35.349 --> 12:37.849
You know, the one where you said
that you were having doubts

12:37.885 --> 12:40.152
about marrying Lois
and you still had thoughts

12:40.187 --> 12:41.320
about marrying me.

12:41.355 --> 12:44.423
Gretchen, I wrote
that a long time ago.

12:44.458 --> 12:46.224
Well, my answer
is yes, Peter.

12:46.260 --> 12:48.593
Yes, I will marry you!

12:48.629 --> 12:50.429
Gretchen,
I am already happily--

12:50.464 --> 12:52.197
moderately hap--
relative-- I am--

12:52.232 --> 12:53.465
I am married.

12:53.500 --> 12:56.101
Oh, then I suppose your wife
is entitled to know

12:56.136 --> 12:57.736
that you were still
in love with me

12:57.771 --> 12:59.471
just days before your wedding.

13:00.474 --> 13:01.540
Blackmail!

13:01.575 --> 13:02.641
Thank you, Cleveland.

13:02.676 --> 13:04.309
And I don't know
what to call the thing

13:04.345 --> 13:05.477
you're doing to me, lady.

13:10.846 --> 13:12.913
Look, Gretchen,
I-I know I wrote you

13:12.948 --> 13:15.549
that letter, and-and-and
I meant it at the time, but...

13:15.584 --> 13:17.517
it was 20 years ago!

13:17.553 --> 13:19.820
I may have had some
doubts before my wedding,

13:19.855 --> 13:21.354
but what guy doesn't?

13:21.390 --> 13:22.522
And now I know

13:22.558 --> 13:24.791
I made the right choice
marrying Lois.

13:24.828 --> 13:27.161
Well, she's a lucky woman,

13:27.196 --> 13:28.795
and I'm sorry for what I said.

13:28.831 --> 13:31.431
I certainly don't want
to cause any trouble for you.

13:31.467 --> 13:33.400
It's just that when I got
this letter, it reminded me

13:33.435 --> 13:35.368
how sweet and funny
you always were.

13:35.404 --> 13:37.637
That's nice,
but I-I should go.

13:37.673 --> 13:39.339
Thanks for not making
fun of me for ordering

13:39.374 --> 13:40.407
a hot chocolate,

13:40.442 --> 13:42.075
and go ahead
and look into Facebook

13:42.111 --> 13:44.244
'cause this is kind of
what it's for.

13:44.279 --> 13:46.847
Wait, before we say
our final good-bye,

13:46.882 --> 13:49.316
what do you say we
have one last hurrah?

13:49.351 --> 13:50.517
I've got two tickets

13:50.552 --> 13:52.652
to a Ray LaMontagne
concert tonight.

13:52.688 --> 13:55.355
Oh, I-I'm not sure
that's a good idea.

13:55.390 --> 13:57.691
It feels a little weird
going out with another lady.

13:57.726 --> 14:00.827
Oh, come on, Peter,
I drove all this way.

14:00.863 --> 14:03.063
Let me go home
with one last good memory,

14:03.098 --> 14:05.132
and then I promise,
you have heard

14:05.167 --> 14:06.600
the last of Gretchen Mercer.

14:06.635 --> 14:08.668
Well, I should
probably say no,

14:08.704 --> 14:10.871
but I've never been
known for my good judgment.

14:10.906 --> 14:12.472
I mean, that's how
I got into trouble

14:12.509 --> 14:13.674
with the Peter Catcher.

14:16.912 --> 14:18.879
Oh, Peter!

14:18.914 --> 14:20.947
Come and get your lollipops!

14:20.983 --> 14:22.048
Lollipops!

14:22.084 --> 14:24.117
Come along, Peter!

14:24.153 --> 14:25.719
Peter, you mustn't.

14:25.754 --> 14:28.088
I've got cream pies.

14:28.123 --> 14:29.723
Trinkle tarts.

14:29.758 --> 14:30.957
Trinkle tarts!

14:36.932 --> 14:39.533
I'm gonna get so molested.

14:46.308 --> 14:49.042
Oh, Peter, you can take
off your hat and jacket.

14:49.077 --> 14:52.012
It's not illegal for two old
friends to go to a concert.

14:52.047 --> 14:53.213
Yeah, I guess you're right.

14:53.248 --> 14:54.981
I mean it's not like
anybody I know would be

14:55.017 --> 14:57.083
at a Ray LaMontagne concert.

14:57.119 --> 14:58.385
Peter!

14:58.420 --> 14:59.420
Where'd he go?

14:59.454 --> 15:00.821
I'm-I'm gonna
keep the hat on.

15:00.856 --> 15:01.856
I'm sorry, Gretchen.

15:01.890 --> 15:02.989
This-this was a mistake.

15:03.025 --> 15:04.391
I just feel too guilty

15:04.426 --> 15:05.759
being out with another woman.

15:05.794 --> 15:07.260
I can't do this to Lois.

15:07.296 --> 15:09.262
Ah, I understand.

15:10.299 --> 15:11.865
Well, I guess there's no shame

15:11.900 --> 15:13.233
in coming in second, huh?

15:13.268 --> 15:14.234
That's right.

15:14.269 --> 15:16.369
Except in, like, wars.

15:16.405 --> 15:19.539
Aw, you are still
funny, sweet Peter.

15:19.575 --> 15:20.674
Yeah, I guess so.

15:20.709 --> 15:21.908
All right, I got to go.

15:21.944 --> 15:23.777
The beard inspector's
coming, anyway.

15:23.812 --> 15:25.512
Uh, sir, where's
your beard?

15:25.547 --> 15:26.747
I'm leaving.
I'm on my way out.

15:27.783 --> 15:29.983
That's my Peter.

15:30.018 --> 15:32.152
<i>That's my Peter.</i>

15:41.230 --> 15:42.796
Wow, looks like
you're actually gonna

15:42.831 --> 15:43.930
get away with this, Stewie.

15:43.966 --> 15:45.899
And you threw a good party.

15:45.934 --> 15:47.467
Yeah, it's getting
pretty wild.

15:47.502 --> 15:48.535
Over in the guest bedroom

15:48.570 --> 15:50.303
there's a girl
pulling a train.

15:50.339 --> 15:52.472
This'll show my dad.

15:52.507 --> 15:54.341
Hey, by the way,
how'd you pay for all this?

15:54.376 --> 15:56.643
I dated Donald Sterling
for two weeks.

15:56.678 --> 15:58.211
He's a good man!

15:58.247 --> 16:00.780
You don't know him
like I know him!

16:02.184 --> 16:03.550
People.
People?

16:03.585 --> 16:06.786
As your rich host, I would
like to say a word if I may.

16:06.822 --> 16:10.223
I cannot tell you how pleased
I am to have finally found

16:10.259 --> 16:11.491
a group of peers with whom

16:11.526 --> 16:13.393
I share so many common
interests...

16:13.428 --> 16:15.528
and here come the people
who live here.

16:17.966 --> 16:19.332
Please let me explain!

16:19.368 --> 16:21.001
I was just worried
you wouldn't accept me

16:21.036 --> 16:22.235
because...

16:22.271 --> 16:24.170
I'm not wealthy
like you are.

16:24.206 --> 16:26.072
Stewie, it's not
that you're poor.

16:26.108 --> 16:28.875
It's that you lied
to us and you're poor.

16:34.249 --> 16:37.017
I'm sorry you lost your
rich friends, Stewie.

16:37.052 --> 16:39.252
Well, that's all right,
I don't need money.

16:39.288 --> 16:41.388
I already have
everything I need.

16:41.423 --> 16:44.090
Excuse me, is one
of you Chadley?

16:44.126 --> 16:45.992
You left your
wallet inside.

16:46.028 --> 16:47.994
Chicka-chickaw!

16:48.030 --> 16:49.729
Well, that "chicka-chickaw"

16:49.765 --> 16:51.865
makes me think
you're not Chadley.

16:51.900 --> 16:52.866
Oh, no!

16:52.901 --> 16:54.601
I chicka-chickawed
too early!

16:59.741 --> 17:01.875
Hey, Lois, you mind if
I cut out of here?

17:01.910 --> 17:03.176
Not at all.
Thanks.

17:03.211 --> 17:04.411
Not to be too intimate,

17:04.446 --> 17:06.046
but I need to have
a bowel movement

17:06.081 --> 17:07.414
and I can't go here.

17:07.449 --> 17:10.951
I can only go at home
or at the Koo Koo Roo.

17:13.889 --> 17:15.055
Hello?

17:15.090 --> 17:16.723
I-Is someone there?

17:16.758 --> 17:20.560
I thought I heard something
over the roar of my tinnitus.

17:20.595 --> 17:22.896
Oh, I'm-I'm sure it's nothing.

17:30.172 --> 17:31.972
Ooh, a text.

17:32.007 --> 17:34.441
"I'm taking care of our problem.

17:34.476 --> 17:35.842
"We'll be together soon.

17:35.877 --> 17:37.210
Love, Gretchen."

17:37.245 --> 17:38.445
Huh.

17:38.480 --> 17:40.280
Meg, you're kind of
a loner psychopath.

17:40.315 --> 17:42.148
What does this mean?

17:42.184 --> 17:44.584
Oh, this woman is
clearly a spurned lover

17:44.619 --> 17:45.852
who's planning to kill Mom.

17:45.887 --> 17:47.821
Ah, thank you.

17:49.992 --> 17:51.291
You're a good dog, Meg.

17:55.864 --> 17:58.565
Well, well, well...

17:58.600 --> 18:01.568
if it isn't the first
Mrs. Griffin.

18:01.603 --> 18:02.702
Gretchen?

18:02.738 --> 18:04.137
What are you doing here?

18:04.172 --> 18:06.206
Making sure Peter can
finally be with me,

18:06.241 --> 18:08.675
which is what
he's always wanted.

18:08.710 --> 18:10.844
Gretchen, it's 3:15
on a workday.

18:10.879 --> 18:12.278
The post office is closed.

18:12.314 --> 18:13.279
Lois!

18:13.315 --> 18:14.481
Gretchen wants to kill you,

18:14.516 --> 18:16.750
and I have a slip that
says we've got a package?

18:16.785 --> 18:18.952
Peter, I'm glad
you're here to see this.

18:18.987 --> 18:21.421
You and I can
finally be together.

18:23.191 --> 18:25.158
Peter, what's going on?!

18:25.193 --> 18:26.826
She's nuts is
what's going on!

18:26.862 --> 18:28.261
I don't want
to be with her!

18:28.296 --> 18:29.262
Oh, yeah?

18:29.297 --> 18:30.630
That's not
what you wrote.

18:30.665 --> 18:31.798
That's right.

18:31.833 --> 18:33.967
I lied about what
was in that letter.

18:34.002 --> 18:35.835
Lois, Lois,
before you read that,

18:35.871 --> 18:37.137
you need to know one thing:

18:37.172 --> 18:40.073
I'm the one throwing out
all your beige bras.

18:40.108 --> 18:42.375
Guys don't
like beige bras.

18:43.545 --> 18:44.644
You told an ex-girlfriend

18:44.679 --> 18:46.613
a week before our wedding

18:46.648 --> 18:48.014
you were having doubts?!

18:48.050 --> 18:49.215
Lois, Lois, listen to me.

18:49.251 --> 18:52.085
Yes, it is true,
just before we got married,

18:52.120 --> 18:53.686
I was having some doubts.

18:53.722 --> 18:55.955
I mean, your family hated me.

18:55.991 --> 18:58.091
I-I didn't think I was good
enough for you.

18:58.126 --> 19:00.160
We were kids, I was scared.

19:00.195 --> 19:01.361
Weren't you?

19:01.396 --> 19:02.896
No, I was in love,

19:02.931 --> 19:05.198
which is what I thought
you were, too.

19:05.233 --> 19:07.233
I was in love, Lois....

19:07.269 --> 19:08.468
and I still am.

19:08.503 --> 19:09.969
Not a day goes by where I don't

19:10.005 --> 19:11.871
thank my lucky stars
for picking you.

19:11.907 --> 19:13.773
It was the best choice
I ever made.

19:13.809 --> 19:15.675
Now, put that gun down,
Gretchen.

19:15.710 --> 19:17.043
You don't have to do this.

19:17.079 --> 19:18.878
That's right, you don't...

19:18.914 --> 19:20.380
because you can have him.

19:20.415 --> 19:21.481
What?!

19:21.516 --> 19:23.116
I'll never forgive you
for this, Peter.

19:23.151 --> 19:24.151
We're through!

19:25.253 --> 19:26.253
Oh, Peter!

19:26.288 --> 19:27.420
I can't wait
for you to meet

19:27.456 --> 19:29.656
the dogs and
the squirrels.

19:29.691 --> 19:31.191
Hey, Gretchen?

19:33.795 --> 19:35.562
Get away from my husband.

19:39.668 --> 19:41.568
Wait, so you're not mad?

19:41.603 --> 19:44.604
No, Peter, I was lying so
she'd let her guard down.

19:44.639 --> 19:46.339
But what about the letter?

19:46.374 --> 19:49.109
Peter, do you remember me
crying at our wedding?

19:49.144 --> 19:50.477
Sure, it's in
all our pictures.

19:50.512 --> 19:51.945
That's doubt.

19:51.980 --> 19:53.847
But there's no doubt anymore.

19:53.882 --> 19:56.549
You're the only man for me,
Peter Griffin.

19:56.585 --> 19:59.450
I love you, Lois.

20:01.299 --> 20:02.869
Oh, Peter.

20:02.893 --> 20:06.235
Now come on, let's get it
on thru a P.O. box.

20:06.753 --> 20:08.214
Peter, this isn't working.

20:08.238 --> 20:09.284
Well I'm at full go.

20:09.308 --> 20:10.694
Are you sure
you're in the right box.

20:10.718 --> 20:11.300
Yes.

20:11.324 --> 20:12.236
Box 528.

20:12.260 --> 20:13.891
Yes, 528.

20:13.915 --> 20:15.395
Alright, just reach in
and grab it.

20:19.914 --> 20:23.466
Wow Mom, I can't believe you
got fired from the Post Office.

20:23.658 --> 20:25.755
Well, they didn't like me
beating up Gretchen

20:25.780 --> 20:27.113
on federal property,

20:27.149 --> 20:29.516
and then after your father
plugged up that P.O. box,

20:29.551 --> 20:31.651
there was a mutual
parting of the ways.

20:31.686 --> 20:33.386
Well, Stewie, I guess
since Lois lost her job,

20:33.421 --> 20:34.587
you're not going
to be able to go

20:34.623 --> 20:36.222
to that fancy
preschool anymore.

20:36.258 --> 20:37.223
Eh, I don't need school.

20:37.259 --> 20:38.224
I'll be fine.

20:38.260 --> 20:39.559
I'll just become
a YouTube star

20:39.594 --> 20:40.594
like Jenna Marbles.

20:40.629 --> 20:41.629
Who's that?

20:41.663 --> 20:42.762
No one knows,
but she's rich,

20:42.797 --> 20:45.098
as rich as
Ray William Johnson.

20:45.133 --> 20:47.233
Who's that?
Nobody knows, but he's rich,

20:47.269 --> 20:49.002
as rich as Bethany Mota

20:49.037 --> 20:50.103
or Marcus Butler

20:50.138 --> 20:52.205
or Ingrid Nilsen.

20:52.240 --> 20:53.773
This?
This is over.

20:53.774 --> 21:00.274
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru